    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nIs there a way to disable specified auto-pairing chars for specified languages in mini.pairs? I know `<C-v>` is helpful, but I think it's kind of redundant. For me, I want to disable auto-pairing of `'` for `Verilog`(in verilog `2'b00` means two bits of 00), but I don't want to disable the whole `mini.pairs` plugin. I hope this can be supported by an API.\r\n\r\nThanks!",
